# Copy to prod.docs.env / dev.docs.env and fill in on the host. Gitignored;
# `chmod 600`. See server.env.example for the general rules.
#
# This gates the documentation site, which serves under /docs. The login flow
# issues root-absolute redirects, so it works there only because Traefik's
# stripPrefix sets X-Forwarded-Prefix and pustaka reads it back (sitePrefix in
# main.go). That is the piece whose absence kept this switched off the last time
# the docs sat behind a prefix -- if the routing ever stops setting the header,
# this layer breaks silently.
#
# WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT COVER. Pustaka's auth guards what Pustaka serves,
# and its allowlist is default-deny including the docs home: signed out you get
# the login page and nothing else. Public are the login routes,
# `/__pustaka/info`, `/robots.txt`, `/favicon.ico`, `/sw.js` and the three
# stylesheets plus webfonts the login page itself loads. Set
# PUSTAKA_AUTH_PUBLIC_HOME=1 below to go back to the older shape, where the docs
# home and all of `/assets/` stay public. The marketing landing page at `/`, plus
# /app (Mission Control) and /api, are different services entirely and are NOT
# affected: the product stays reachable.

# --- The master switch. Unset or 0 => the layer is off and the server -------
# --- behaves exactly as it did before, byte for byte. -----------------------
# 1 turns it on; unset or 0 leaves it off.
PUSTAKA_AUTH=

# --- One shared credential pair, not accounts. The server REFUSES TO START ---
# --- if the layer is on and either of these is empty. ------------------------
PUSTAKA_AUTH_USER=
PUSTAKA_AUTH_PASS=

# --- Signs the session cookie. Generate your own: --------------------------
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# Leave it blank and the server invents a random one per process, which means
# every deploy and every restart signs everyone out.
#
# Do NOT copy the committed default another project ships in its compose file.
# A secret in version control is not a secret.
PUSTAKA_AUTH_SECRET=

# --- Session lifetime. Any Go duration: 720h, 24h, 30m. --------------------
# 720h is a sensible month.
PUSTAKA_AUTH_TTL=

# --- Secure cookie flag: auto | 1 | 0. --------------------------------------
#
# USE 1 HERE, NOT auto. This is the one setting inherited from the sibling
# project whose guidance does not survive this topology.
#
# `auto` resolves to `r.TLS != nil` (sitePrefix's neighbour, main.go:785) -- it
# asks whether THIS process terminated TLS, and it does not read
# X-Forwarded-Proto. In these stacks TLS ends at the edge and the tunnel carries
# plain HTTP, so r.TLS is always nil and `auto` silently ships a session cookie
# with NO Secure flag on a site that is HTTPS-only from the browser's side.
#
# Nothing fails visibly: you log in, it works, and the cookie is merely one
# plain-HTTP request away from travelling in the clear. Like the dashboard's
# GAOS_COOKIE_SECURE, the flag is env-driven and never scheme-derived.
PUSTAKA_AUTH_SECURE=1

# --- Scope of the gate. Unset (recommended) => even the docs home needs a ---
# --- session, and the only public assets are the login page's own. ---------
# 1 puts the docs home and all of /assets/ back on the public side, which is
# how this behaved before. Anything other than 1/0/true/false/yes/no/on/off is
# a startup error, not a guess.
PUSTAKA_AUTH_PUBLIC_HOME=
